# Fix the product, not the server

This is a product. Issues are resolved by changing GET/SET, and the operator re-running them. Do not change the server to make the symptom go away.

- SSH is investigation-only: Read logs, query state, confirm what GET/SET did.
- Never apply fixes over SSH: Do not modify host files, units, containers, directories, users, packages, or runtime state.
- Fix the source: Update playbooks, roles, generators, or catalog inputs so the next GET/SET produces the correct state.
- Exception: Only an explicit user instruction authorizes direct server modifications. "Fix it" is not sufficient.